<title>MEXICO: Mexico to restart port concession auctions - paper.</title>
<headline>Mexico to restart port concession auctions - paper.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico will soon restart to auction off concessions to run 15 ports, the daily newspaper Reforma said Monday.</p>
<p>Citing Eduardo Aspero, coordinator of the government's port concession sell-off, Reforma said the concession rights for four ports could be put on the block as soon as November.</p>
<p>Aspero named the ports of Topolobampo, Guaymas, Tuxpan and Mazatlan as ones that could soon be auctioned off, Reforma said. Earlier this year, concession auctions dried up without any explanation.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530.</p>
